`@web/graphics` will give you WebGL2 rendering for games, simulations and 3D
applications. It keeps WebGL's model of shaders, buffers, textures and draw
calls, with Moth types in place of JavaScript overloads and numeric constants.

The package is registered but doesn't expose any functions yet. Its first API
waits for binding features that let it accept a `@web/canvas` canvas and upload
vertex and pixel data cleanly.

Use @../canvas (@web/canvas) for 2D drawing today.

For the package scope, the planned areas and what the first API needs, see
@#graphics (@web/graphics advanced).
